From d08b4fcab47511162f8eaaa98ad51c689c9fffc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:31:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the dashboard's Current Requests widget work via Caddy's
 admin API

Adds Settings > Caddy Settings > Caddy API > "Caddy admin API URL", an
optional address (e.g. caddy.example.com:2019) Caddy Manager uses to
read live stats from Caddy's own admin API.

New caddy_api.py fetches GET /reverse_proxy/upstreams and sums
num_requests/fails across all upstreams, the same approach community
dashboard widgets for Caddy (e.g. homepage's) already use. The
Dashboard's Current Requests widget -- previously a hardcoded "83" --
now shows the real live count, falling back to "N/A" when the API URL
isn't configured or Caddy can't be reached, rather than erroring.
upstreams_total and failed_requests are also computed into the
dashboard's stats context for future widgets, though not shown yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
